   "title": "Step 2 of the balanced-source route: carry the colour through the shot",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## What this graph does\n\nOne approved colour frame (the **palette still** from step 1) is carried through a 124-frame section of the shot by **MiniMax H3** in reference-to-video mode, with Alibaba's **Fun ControlNet** holding the model to the edge map of every frame.\n\n**Inputs.** `context.mp4`: the source section, 768 \u00d7 576, 24 fps, 124 frames. `control.mp4`: its Canny edge map, frame for frame. `palette.png`: the approved still, given three times (pictures 1 to 3) so the reference weighs more than the prompt.\n\n**Output.** `t185_h3_*.mp4`, a colour video at 768 \u00d7 576. It is a **colour donor only**: in the next step its brightness is thrown away and only its Cb/Cr is used, on the scan's own luma, at the scan's full resolution."
   ],
   "color": "#3b3b2e",
   "bgcolor": "#5a5a3a"
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    0,
    356
   ],
   "size": [
    560,
    278
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 24,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "What should and should not happen",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "**Should.** Every person, garment and object takes the colour it has in the palette still, and keeps it through the movement. The picture follows the edge map exactly: same framing, same timing, same gestures.\n\n**Should not.** New objects, changed faces or hands, colour crossing an edge into the background, a palette that drifts between sections, flicker. A frame that shows any of these is not used to train the adapter (step 3): every frame is lined up against the source and used only if its brightness matches within 1.5 px.\n\n**Settings that matter.** Seed 0, 20 steps, `res_multistep` / `simple`, ControlNet strength 1.0 over the whole run. Sections overlap, and the seam is placed in a calm passage."
   ],
   "color": "#3b3b2e",
   "bgcolor": "#5a5a3a"
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    0,
    674
   ],
   "size": [
    560,
    126
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 25,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "Hardware",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "This is a **video** step: MiniMax H3 at 768 \u00d7 576 for 124 frames wants an NVIDIA card with 24 GB of VRAM or more (RTX 3090/4090; 32 GB on an RTX 5090 is comfortable) and 64 GB of system RAM, and takes 20 to 45 minutes a section. It opens in Comfy Cloud for reading, but running it there is a paid, long job; the single-frame graphs are the ones meant for Cloud."
   ],
   "color": "#3b3b2e",
   "bgcolor": "#5a5a3a"
  },
